    - target: {fileID: 2567914334466426269, guid: bcefd6bd51ce47b438fb5d83f536cd3c,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: description
      value: Images usually hold data in 4 different channels, red, green, blue and
        alpha, which is usually used for transparency. However, if you don't need
        all of them, you can also store different data in them. However, this requies
        the correct project sync between the shader.
