    - target: {fileID: 9014058579521311922, guid: bcefd6bd51ce47b438fb5d83f536cd3c,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: description
      value: Just sampling the pixels of textures results in noise, especially when
        scaling it down. Incorporating surrounding pixels makes it better. These
        can be precalculated and stored. Therefore, blurry, low resolution versions
        of the textures are used to make it smoother.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 9020381124328112330, guid: bcefd6bd51ce47b438fb5d83f536cd3c,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: serializedProgramAsset
      value: 
      objectReference: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd0b187544328de4da8b1b12545c3a4c,
        type: 2}
    - target: {fileID: 9038117583529453208, guid: bcefd6bd51ce47b438fb5d83f536cd3c,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: 'Lights can be combined by simply adding their values together. However,
        this can result in values becoming larger than 1.


        The traditional
        method involves using values in such a way that the output is always in the
        range 0...1.


        Meanwhile, more advanced models use realistic brightness
        values and camera exposure models with tone mappers. HDR monitors are also
        able to display more colors and post processing applies bloom to higher values.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
